WEBVTT

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.460
Sis-sis, you rock!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.670
<i>Gosh...</i>

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.090
<i>Chieri really </i>is<i> amazing.</i>

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.520
Well, I suppose they're not half bad.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.440
Those girls...

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.530
They shouldn't have learned
this song yet. When did they...?

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.530
Honestly, they wouldn't get off my case.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.630
Ow...

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.750
You girls...

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:11.590
What are you doing?

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.760
P-Please let us observe your lessons!

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.510
W-We'll stay out of the way!

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.510
Please!

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.470
They were so insistent.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.940
When I let them have a corner of the
practice room, they were positively ecstatic.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.000
Ready, set, here we go!

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.040
AKB0048!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.840
Tomochin, we'll leave without you.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:20.680
Wait up!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.680
Great job out there!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.810
That was nerve-wracking.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.810
My knees were shaking.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.730
Both of you were incredible!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.980
You put on a great show.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:32.730
Totally!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.730
My Sis-sis is the best!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.570
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.900
You were great too, Chieri.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.740
Really?

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.410
Mimori-san, you were just <i>oozing</i> pheromones.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.240
Oh dear, you think so?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.120
You did great, Megu.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.790
Megu...

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.670
What are you doing?

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.550
There's a news report on the members who went to the peace ceremony.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.050
Let us see!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.850
AKB0048 brought courage to the
citizens with their heavenly voices.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.610
It cut out.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.440
DES is interfering with the broadcast.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.530
Still, Takamina-san looked awesome!

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.910
You're her biggest supporter, aren't you?

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.320
Well, not exactly...

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.280
Kanata-san.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:28.870
Yes?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.080
They should be back right about now.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.880
Oh no!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.840
Sis-sis...

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.930
She must really love Takamina-san.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.220
Yeah. We should go welcome them, too.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.390
Good idea.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.480
Takamina-san!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.450
Welcome back!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.860
Thanks.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.620
Did you put on a good show while we were gone?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:11.370
You bet!

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.000
Somebody's confident. Watch out, I'll be checking the recording later.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:15.830
Ow!

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.630
Welcome back!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.590
Now, let's begin the meeting.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.590
Tundrastar, the location of our next concert, is fully under the Entertainment Ban.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:33.980
The fans there are clamoring for us, but conflict with DES is inevitable.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.100
This will be an unpredictable guerrilla concert.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.650
A guerrilla concert...

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.730
...on a planet where entertainment is completely banned...

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.570
...and conflict is inevitable.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:46.320
Therefore, we will be taking special measures for this concert.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.490
Kanata,

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.280
Yes!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.070
Mimori,

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:49.820
Yes!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.530
Megumi,

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.580
Yes!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.910
and everyone in the 77th generation. You will be performing as stand-ins.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:58.080
Huh?

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.790
You mean for the guerrilla concert?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.550
Wow.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.430
We'll be going on stage!

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.630
Hold on!

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.390
Why the 77th generation?

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.390
Why am I the only one from the 76th?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:18.850
Can the 76th generation perform today's set list?

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.570
Though they were not all selected, everyone from the 77th generation still practiced.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.320
Meanwhile, what was the 76th generation doing?

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.030
I believe I told you before.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:35.490
You have to practice. That's all you can do.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.130
Takamina-san!

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.880
Do you have a minute?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.350
Kanata.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.100
Thank goodness I caught you.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.850
You can trust me as your stand-in!

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.650
I'll give it my all!

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.030
Um... right. I'm counting on you.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:07.940
Right on!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.200
Kanata!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.160
The others are already heading to the station.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.490
Got it!

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.290
Well, good luck with your future missions!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.120
Takamina.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.670
Was I acting weird at all?

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.550
Huh?

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:34.930
What would the original Takamina-san have done at a time like this?

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:40.980
I suppose she'd smile and give her teammate some pep talk.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.570
There's so much that I'm not sure of anymore.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:51.570
I guess I didn't have my best
Takamina face on back there.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.660
I can't stand this!

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.620
Don't cry, Hazuki.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:04.790
But we became understudies way before they did!

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.550
Come on, cheer up.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.550
Kanata-san...

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.880
As long as you work hard, you'll get your chance.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:17.350
Just don't let the next opportunity slip by, okay?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.310
You're right. Next time, for sure.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.310
Right.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:25.770
Are you sure?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.440
Then what about you, Kanata-senpai?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:34.910
You've worked your hardest as an
understudy, but you never caught a break.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.580
If I were you, I'd be too ashamed to remain in 00!

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.660
What?!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.960
Sonata, stay out of this.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.170
I don't believe you!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.340
I'm officially calling you Nasty from now on!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.170
Suzuko?!

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.050
That was a headbutt.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.640
That means it hurt me as much as it hurt you,

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.100
so I won't apologize.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:05.140
However, you need to apologize to Kanata-san.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.440
Megu, let's go.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.520
We're really sorry. Really.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.120
Megumi-san had a hard head.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.080
Th-There's a bump!

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.290
Pain, pain, go away to Megumi!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.750
Thanks, Suzuko.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.460
Kanata-san...

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.090
But you didn't have to.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.840
I understand how they feel.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.130
We were pretty shaken back then, too.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.050
Back when Youko...

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.100
I mean, when Sae was promoted before the rest of us,

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.560
we pretty much panicked.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.560
Sae-san was from the 76th generation?

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.980
That's right.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.570
But that girl's just too nice.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.530
She was so apologetic.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.660
In the end, <i>we</i> were the ones who felt bad.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.740
Yeah.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.580
Well, Chef Papa's dinner is waiting for us.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.870
Let's head back.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.040
Okay!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.080
I'm starving!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.750
I wonder what we're having tonight.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.690
Being a stand-in for a concert, huh?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.480
I hope I can handle it.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.320
Don't be so negative.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.570
Huh?

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.950
If you don't perform with confidence,

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:40.410
you'll be disrespecting the girls who weren't selected.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.410
I've thought this for a while now,

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.410
but you're actually pretty kind, aren't you?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.210
Okay. I'll be confident.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.080
I'm pretty nervous, though.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.170
Hey, when you get nervous, don't your teeth itch?

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.050
Righ' back 'ere.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.300
See?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.600
H-Hey, Chieri!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.110
I thought, with that big mouth of
yours, a mandarin would fit right in.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.150
Don't be ridiculous!

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.610
Gosh, Chieri!

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.490
<i>How have you been?</i>

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:25.410
<i>I've just been chosen to appear in concert as a stand-in.</i>

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.910
<i>That's one more step towards my dream, which I know you're against...</i>

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:34.420
"...but someday, I want you to see me on stage, Mamoru."

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:35.540
"That's why..."

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.010
Peeking is rude, you two.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.340
It's a letter!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.470
And to a boy, no less!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.970
Why you...!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.560
Yuuka's gone crazy!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.600
Yuuka?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:54.230
First, we'll arrive in the target sector on the <i>Katyusha</i> and gather intel.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.190
Afterwards, we'll descend to
Tundrastar on the <i>Flying Get</i>.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:03.070
With that said, let's go and meet the fans we love!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.080
It's been a while since we slept in here!

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.250
Let's have a good performance.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.760
Megumi-san...

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.880
Okay!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.550
Time to start practice.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.100
What? But we just left.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.850
That's no excuse. There are practice rooms on the <i>Katyusha</i>, too.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.140
We're gonna work till we drop!

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:34.440
Kanata-san's all fired up.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:39.070
She's gotta show off in front of her beloved Takamina-san.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.440
What was that?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.530
You can join us—

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.490
No thank you.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:47.990
Megumi...

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.450
Bye-bye, Nasty!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.920
<i>I love you, I love you so much.</i>

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.460
<i>I'll chase you with all my might.</i>

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.090
<i>I love you...</i>

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.510
Why aren't you practicing with the others?

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.470
Youko...

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:11.600
It's Sae. I'm not Youko any—

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.890
You <i>are</i> still Youko!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.690
What's wrong, Megu?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:16.810
You're acting strange.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.980
What do you mean, "strange"?

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.280
You couldn't possibly understand me, Youko.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:28.320
You're the only 76th generation
understudy who's become a successor.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.870
We used to be together all the time, but now I never see you.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.870
There's no way you'd understand.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:37.750
Megu...

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.750
I'm sorry.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.300
Why are you apologizing?!

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.920
Good question.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.890
Don't get caught hanging out with an understudy,

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.060
Sae-san.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.390
Megu.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.770
Whoa! That's a lot!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.230
Orine, aren't you on a diet?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:07.200
I lost some weight from the intense practices, so I quit.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.240
Now <i>that's</i> a feast.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.660
Girls, do you have a moment?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.380
We've received intel from the WOTA who arrived before us.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.090
The WOTA?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:27.800
They're the ones who saved us at the handshake event, right?

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:34.810
According to their report, DES has called in reinforcements from neighboring planets.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:41.400
It seems the D.G.T.O. wants to take
this opportunity to capture all of 00.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.190
That's crazy!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.740
We don't have enough combat-ready members or LAS to face them.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.160
For everyone's safety, the concert is canceled.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.410
We'll do it!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.780
Takamina...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.040
But the danger you'll face—

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.330
Who cares about a little danger?

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:04.550
We'll put our lives on the line to perform for the people who are counting on us!

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.380
That's what AKB0048 is all about!

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.180
I'm in, too!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.970
I'll follow Takamina-san to
the ends of the universe!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.600
You too?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.930
Kanata...

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.190
Kanata deserves the name of Takamina.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:28.400
<i>If I graduate, she'll be promoted.</i>

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.150
<i>But...</i>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.360
A DES attack?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.200
They're early.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.620
Must be the welcoming party.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.580
All hands, battle stations!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.830
Roger!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.080
What should we...

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.290
Change into battle gear and stand by!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:42.880
Let's go!

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.540
Roger!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:46.960
There are four enemy craft.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.840
Takamina! Sayaka! Sae!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:49.630
Right!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.760
Divert the enemy as far away from the planet as you can.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.600
Meanwhile, we'll move the <i>Katyusha</i> somewhere safe.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.010
Here we go!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:57.720
Okay!

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.610
Once you attract their attention, move away from the <i>Katyusha</i>!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:14.570
Roger!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.500
<i>Am I really doing my job as captain?</i>

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.750
<i>Am I a captain like the original
Takamina, Takahashi Minami-san,</i>

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:30.880
<i>whom the other members respected and obeyed?</i>

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:31.720
Takamina! Over there!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.430
They're firing on us?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.850
Oh no! The sub-engines!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.230
Tsubasa-san! I'm launching, too.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:48.820
Takamina's not herself today.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.110
Okay.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:52.320
Can any other members pilot an LAS?

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.990
Please, let me go!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:54.820
Kanata?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:58.910
My father taught me how to operate the base-type.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.200
I can act as combat service support.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.210
But you're still...

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.210
Please!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.920
Very well.

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.130
I'm going in.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.380
Block 7, emergency lockdown!

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:19.430
Takamina!

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:23.810
Are you okay?

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.600
Two new craft are approaching.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.320
That type...

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.150
Takamina, we're not getting anywhere.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.030
Your orders?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.400
Takamina?

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.490
Sayaka, watch out!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.550
What the—

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.000
Is he—

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.510
No!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.170
Takamina!

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.380
Takamina!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.570
Takamina-san!

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:13.860
Kanata...

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.530
Takamina! Takamina!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.330
Takamina unit, pod secured.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.910
Requesting retrieval.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.450
Understood. Launching recovery shuttle.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.870
Wait, Kanata! One of those craft is manned!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.920
Don't you dare!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.920
You're trying to take away the people I care about again!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.880
You bastards!

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.810
The Kirara...

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.890
are illuminating Kanata.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:56.610
They're proclaiming Kanata... as Takahashi Minami.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:02.490
Takamina-san!

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>No...</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.250
<i>That's not... my name.</i>

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.750
Takamina-san! Takamina-san!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.630
Takamina-san!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.970
You're finally awake.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:31.600
I hope you made up for the sleep you've been missing due to your schedule.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.770
You were unconscious so long.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.610
That girl wouldn't stop worrying about you.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:40.530
She wanted to stay until you woke up,

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.120
but I figured she'd be drained from her first battle,

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.120
so I sent her away.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:53.130
I couldn't protect Takamina-san.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.260
You weren't yourself today.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:03.300
What happened to "calm, kind, and just"?

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.970
I... don't want to give up yet.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:14.150
My singing isn't great, and my dancing is only so-so.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:18.530
I had no confidence and nothing to be proud of.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:25.370
But when I was selected as Takamina the 5th, I finally gained some self-confidence.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.700
I want to stay as Takamina.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.460
I want to stay in 00.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.880
I don't want to graduate.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:39.420
But...

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:44.550
But as long as I'm here, Kanata will remain an understudy.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:53.100
That girl works so hard and adores me so much.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.900
She looks at me with those
sparkling, determined eyes.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.400
Yet...

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:06.110
I'm crushing her dream for the sake of my own.

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.160
What's wrong with that?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.330
We all care about those girls.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:21.090
But your dream is what matters above all.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.380
Your <i>own</i> dream.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.340
My own... dream...

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:31.890
Everyone in 00 is chasing the same dream.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:36.350
Still, that dream means something different to each of us.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:41.820
Dreams only match perfectly in fairy tales.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.740
Your dream belongs to you alone.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.360
What's wrong with that?

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.210
I have to...

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:58.330
I have to... I have to...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.300
I have to get stronger.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:05.630
I have to work harder.

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.130
I have to...

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:09.260
I have to!

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:24.650
The stars that shine in the night sky

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:24.650
yoru no sora kagayaku hoshi wa

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:27.240
lie billions of lightyears away.

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:27.230
nanoku kounen no kanata

00:22:27.230 --> 00:22:28.030
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:22:27.240 --> 00:22:29.780
Even if the depths of despair

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:29.780
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.330
should cast an endless shadow,

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:32.320
mugen no yami to nattemo

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:33.240
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:34.950
the truth will make itself heard.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:34.950
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:37.580
Who shall be the one to receive

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:37.580
jikan no kawa ni takushita

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:39.960
the message of light

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:39.960
sono hikari no messeeji

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:42.340
set adrift on the river of time?

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:42.330
uketoru mono wa dare dai?

00:22:42.580 --> 00:22:45.290
hito wa umarete hito wa shinde yuku

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:47.470
People are born, and people die.

00:22:45.290 --> 00:22:47.460
hito wa umarete hito wa shinde yuku

00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:47.920
nikutai wa horobiru yo

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:51.930
Our bodies don't last forever.

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:51.930
nikutai wa horobiru yo

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:57.600
Those who rise back up from the ashes

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:57.600
hai no naka kara yomigaeru mono wa

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:03.320
give passion to the next generation.

00:22:57.600 --> 00:23:03.310
jounetsu tsugi no sedai e

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:06.690
yume wa reincarnation

00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:06.690
Dreams are like reincarnation.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:11.620
Like déjà vu, my distant memories

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:11.610
nando demo deja vu no you na

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.280
tooi kioku

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.280
keep coming back to me.

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:17.490
marude reincarnation

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:17.500
It's just like reincarnation.

00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:21.870
ima mo mata muishiki no uchi ni

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:21.880
With my head still in the clouds,

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:26.040
dokoka e hashitteru

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:26.050
I'm running off somewhere again.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:33.050
Will enough tears make me give up?

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:33.050
ikutsume no namida de akirameru no ka?

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:39.100
Will enough lives make my dream come true?

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:39.100
ikutsume no inochi de kanau mono nano ka?

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.570
This is what people are like
under the Entertainment Ban.

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:52.330
Please, let me do this!

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:54.820
I promise I won't make a fool of myself!

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:57.620
Yay! Snow, snow, snow!

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.950
You've convinced me.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:00.950
- Emotion Relation-
